libgphoto2_port/vusb: show the virtual camera without a storage while it is locked

A locked phone, or one not set to file transfer, answers PTP but lists its
storage without a medium: GetStorageIDs returns an ID whose logical part is 0,
which ptp_getstorageids() filters out, so the root holds no storage folder and
Framehive asks the person to unlock the device (CLI-013.15). The virtual PTP
camera of the `vusb` port driver (configure --enable-vusb) always lists its
storage 0x00010001. With this patch, while the file VCAMERA_LOCKED_WHILE names
exists, it lists 0x00010000 instead, so a test can lock the camera by creating
that file and unlock it by removing it. Without VCAMERA_LOCKED_WHILE nothing
changes.

It changes only the `vusb` driver, which Framehive installs outside the iolib
folder that the library loads by default. It is written to be offered upstream.

Applied by flake.nix to nixpkgs' libgphoto2.

--- a/libgphoto2_port/vusb/vcamera.c
+++ b/libgphoto2_port/vusb/vcamera.c
@@ -829,6 +829,17 @@
 	return 1;
 }
 
+/* Like a locked phone: while the file VCAMERA_LOCKED_WHILE names exists, the
+ * storage is listed without a medium (logical storage ID 0).
+ */
+static int
+locked (void) {
+	const char	*path = getenv ("VCAMERA_LOCKED_WHILE");
+	struct stat	stbuf;
+
+	return path && !stat (path, &stbuf);
+}
+
 static int
 ptp_getstorageids_write(vcamera *cam, ptpcontainer *ptp) {
 	unsigned char 	*data;
@@ -841,7 +852,7 @@
 
 	data = malloc(200);
 
-	sids[0] = 0x00010001;
+	sids[0] = locked () ? 0x00010000 : 0x00010001;
 	x = put_32bit_le_array (data, sids, 1);
 
 	ptp_senddata (cam, 0x1004, data, x);
